<title>USA: Delta Q1 load factor up, cargo revs down.</title>
<headline>Delta Q1 load factor up, cargo revs down.</headline>
<dateline>MONROE, La. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines Inc on Thursday attributed an 8 percent increase in first quarter revenues to a 12 percent rise in revenue passenger miles.</p>
<p>The increase was offset by a 5 percent reduction in the passenger mile yield, and cargo revenue fell 4 percent to $124 million, the company said.</p>
<p>Passenger load factor for the quarter rose to 73.9 percent, compared with 68.1 percent for the year-ago quarter, the carrier said.</p>
</text>
